<title>UK: UK CORYTON OIL REFINERY CRACKER RE-STARTS ON FRIDAY.</title>
<headline>UK CORYTON OIL REFINERY CRACKER RE-STARTS ON FRIDAY.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The catalytic cracker at the BP/Mobil U.K. Coryton oil refinery has re-started and is expected to be fully operational by Saturday, said a BP company spokesman on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;The re-streaming process started today and it should be fully operational by tomorrow,&quot; said the spokesman.</p>
<p>The company had originally hoped for a restart of the 60,000 barrel per day cracker earlier this week after it had been shut down last week due to a technical problem.</p>
<p>The Coryton refinery has a crude oil distillation capacity of about 180,000 bpd.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
